  "prefLabel": "Env-A 402.03 Limitations on Individual Sources for Class B Major Sources",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 402.03 Limitations on Individual Sources for Class B Major Sources. Pursuant to RSA 125-D:3, I(e), unless otherwise authorized by RSA 125-D:3, I(f) relative to 2 or more sources under a single ownership, each class B major source shall have an average emission rate not to exceed 1.6 pounds of SO2 per million BTU heat input, equivalent to no. 6 oil with 1.5% sulfur by weight, which is 75 percent of the baseline average emission rate for class B major sources.\n\nSource. #10288, eff 3-19-13; ss by #13641, eff 5-23-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a400.html"
}
